      "reason": "The local array 'unsigned int data[2]' is never initialized in this function, yet it is passed as the IPI message payload to the VPU/SCP firmware. Uninitialized kernel stack contents are sent to the co-processor (information leak), and the firmware acts on garbage parameters, which can cause undefined decoder behavior."
    }
  ],
  "suggested_fix": "Initialize the array before use (e.g. 'unsigned int data[2] = { 0 };' or memset), and fill in the actual parameters the firmware expects for a single-core decode start. Additionally, validate the bitstream length so that buf[nal_start_idx] stays within bs->size."
}

